# Files that must NOT be uploaded to the deployment.
#
# vercel.json sets `outputDirectory: "."`, so the repo root IS the static root:
# every path that exists in the repo is fetchable over HTTP unless excluded here.
# Verified against production before this file existed —
# https://cardle.lol/supabase/migrations/012-username-blocklist.sql returned 200
# with the full seed list, and /DESIGN.md returned all 392 KB of internal notes.
#
# That mattered most for the username blocklist. src/state/auth.js argues at
# length that the availability check must return a bare boolean so the word list
# "cannot be recited" — and the list was sitting in a world-readable .sql file
# the whole time. A deploy config quietly undid an RLS design.
#
# NOT excluded, deliberately:
#   src/        the browser imports these modules directly — this is a no-build
#               project, so the source IS the bundle. It is readable by design.
#   public/     the site itself.
#   robots.txt, sitemap.xml, vercel.json, package.json
#               served, or needed by the platform.

# Database schema, RLS policies, security-definer function bodies, and the
# blocklist seed list.
supabase/

# Internal design notes and the numbered decision log.
DESIGN.md
GAME_PLAN.md

# Test suites and the local dev server. Neither runs on Vercel, and the dev
# server has no business being readable as a hint about local tooling.
tests/
tools/

# Editor/agent scratch, in case any ever lands in the repo root.
.claude/
